This is an example of using the new extensible error reporting mechanism in the ACS, which is used by MacApp. ProgramBreak and ProgramReport is piped throw the currently installed CReporter. There are three examples of error reporting in CReporter:1. using DebugStr/dout (the default reporter)2. using an Alert3. using a log window.To see each in action,  choose one of the reporters in "ReporterExample" menu item and then choose "New..." in the file menu. New is supposed to and will fail (MakeNewDocument is returning NULL).  You can see each of the different reporters in action by doing this.The code for making a CReporter straight forward. All you need to do is subclass CReporter and override the virtual method OutputMessage. When you instantiate your subclass it automatically becomes the current CReporter and all the debugging output is sent to it. When the instance of your CReporter is deleted, the previous CReporter is reinstalled automatically.